<title>USA: U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. rice weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA rice export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Sales of 23,200 MT were down 44 percent from the week earlier and 39 percent from the 4-week average.  The primary buyers were the Netherlands (6,300 MT), Peru (5,000 MT), Haiti (2,800 MT), Mexico (2,600 MT, of which 2,500 MT was rough), Nicaragua (1,200 MT), and Colombia (1,000 MT--all rough).</p>
<p>Exports of 41,600 MT were 37 percent above the week earlier and 28 percent over the 4-week average.  The major destination was Turkey (15,500 MT), South Africa (7,600 MT), the Dominican Republic (4,000 MT), Ghana (3,200 MT), Mexico (3,000 MT), and Liberia (2,200 MT).</p>
</text>
